Package: bigcurve
Title: Adaptive Densification of Lines for Map Projections
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Michael D.", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Simon", "Wotherspoon", role = "ctb",
           comment = "wrote SGAT::trackMdpts, the ancestor of the spherical midpoint used here"),
    person("Mike", "Bostock", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of the 'd3-geo' adaptive resampling method ported here; see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: Densify lines adaptively, as required by the curvature a map
    projection imposes on them. Edges are read as great circle arcs, and
    vertices are inserted along them only where the projected curve
    deviates from a straight chord by more than a tolerance measured on the
    map, following the adaptive resampling scheme of 'd3-geo'
    <https://github.com/d3/d3-geo>. Projections are computed with the
    'PROJ' library, so any coordinate reference system it supports can be a
    target. Inputs can be coordinate matrices, segment meshes or vertex pool
    topology from 'wkpool', and edges shared by neighbouring polygons
    receive identical new vertices.
